From f8a8ff8d67254702254a7aef1b548da7ef020a3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:15:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): a shipped build ignores CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE; a
 field-engine verdict names its engine

The carry-engine switch (#637) is honoured only in builds with debug
assertions (dev and test profiles); a release build never reads the
variable and always carries stock on the column engine, so one project
gets the same verdict on every machine. The read is the pure
engine_from_switch(value, honoured), pinned in the shipped configuration.

Wherever the field engine does judge, the post gate's visible line, the
setup sheet's SIM line and the Deviate readout say so. Nothing is added
on the column engine: no golden or shipped verdict text moves.

Fixes #1168

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
